ut if you\u2019ve been waiting to back this ride, now\u2019s the time!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/339646881/apocalyptic-record-for-werewolf-the-apocalypse-20th-ann-ed\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...se-20th-ann-ed</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T14:35:44-07:00","id":1464793,"title":"","content":"And done! What an amazing send off to a fantastic game line. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T01:16:48-07:00","id":1464836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460695-the-apocalyptic-record-ks-has-begun?p=1464693#post1464693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, you were the ST! I thought your character (as in your PC) called him Yurizinho... hahahahaha... awesome!!!<br /> <br /> I can see other Lords spending Willpower not to laugh... kkkkk...</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a PC, actually. A huge spending on Backgrounds can do wonders. Of course it had its share of drawbacks, but it was fun to watch the other Lords trying not to laugh as if their lives depended on it (which they did).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:24:42-07:00","id":1464846,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts on the previews as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> If I have an issue with something, it has to be the 'Hey, maybe we could use a different kind of thinking? Oh wait,NOPE!' sections. With the Mockery Breeds, it made sense. But once we got to using Weaver as an ally or curing a BSD it got old.<br /> <br /> A huge part of WtA is that the old ways CAN be useful, but new ways and perspectives are extremely necessary to fix things. The two philodox section parts felt needlessly regressive, especially as Hestia was painted as an intolerant arse and the ST hooks section made it clear there -is- no way to cure a BSD and Wretch was just acting. While I understand the reason why no cured BSDs exist in W20, there could have been a third 'maybe Wretch did not return to his Hive that eagerly after being treated so well' or something like that. A chance or a possibility. After all, the theurge chapter had a fomor being cored and Bat being redeemed.<br /> <br /> Please note, these are minor gripes about an otherwise great book.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 10-22-2021, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:38:24-07:00","id":1464848,"title":"","content":"I've always felt that if a Wyrm servant can't be redeemed, then something must be very wrong with Gaia. It does make the Wyrm seems like it is right, as its servants have stronger loyalty to it than Gaians can even dream to have.<br /> <br /> This has always been quite serious to me.<br /> <br /> Also, edit out the extra 's' on the closing box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:43:29-07:00","id":1464849,"title":"","content":"Yeah, maybe Glen Seize-Trouble is right. I'd like to think so, even if he got a little scared upon first real contact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:50:41-07:00","id":1464852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460695-the-apocalyptic-record-ks-has-begun?p=1464848#post1464848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always felt that if a Wyrm servant can't be redeemed, then something must be very wrong with Gaia. It does make the Wyrm seems like it is right, as its servants have stronger loyalty to it than Gaians can even dream to have.<br /> <br /> This has always been quite serious to me.<br /> <br /> Also, edit out the extra 's' on the closing box.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, fixed it.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah. In revised, you COULD redeem a BSD, there was even a rite for it. It is only in W20 where there is an EXTREMELY hard no to it. I find it interesting because W20 has been more allowing. But then again, the way BSDs function in W20 is -very- different from 2nd ed and revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T21:41:19-07:00","id":1464965,"title":"","content":"Everything in the AR except Chapter 6 and the plot hooks sections are in character. Whatever the characters and storytellers in those section believe isn't objective truth and shouldn't be treated as such.<br /> <br /> I would draw your attention to the Philodox story hooks, which does say &quot;Even though no fallen Garou has ever redeemed doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s impossible. The time for such a miracle may be in the face of the coming Apocalypse.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460695-the-apocalyptic-record-ks-has-begun?p=1464852#post1464852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is only in W20 where there is an EXTREMELY hard no to it. I find it interesting because W20 has been more allowing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit to add: I'm confused why you think W20 has an 'extremely hard no'. Not only do we have the words in the Philodox chapter as I've included above, W20 Umbra the Velvet Shadow included a BSD in Erebus working its way towards possible redemption. If anything, W20 has an extremely hard 'MAYBE' to it - ie, it's up to individual tables to decie if that's a story they want to tell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 10-23-2021, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T21:48:56-07:00","id":1464967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460695-the-apocalyptic-record-ks-has-begun?p=1464848#post1464848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always felt that if a Wyrm servant can't be redeemed, then something must be very wrong with Gaia. It does make the Wyrm seems like it is right, as its servants have stronger loyalty to it than Gaians can even dream to have.<br /> <br /> This has always been quite serious to me.<br /> <br /> Also, edit out the extra 's' on the closing box.</div> </div> </div> </div>I clearly have been running things poorly because I've always used the Rite of Cleansing as a kind of exorcist ability. Anything prior to becoming a full-on Formori, you're capable of being healed and living Gaian again. After you're a Formori, you're not really a person anymore and lack free will.<br /> <br /> Part of why Black Spiral Dancers aren't fond of vampires. They just aren't POSSESSED the same way proper Formori are supposed to be. Which amusingly, means I treat the Formori like the Heartless from Kingdom Hearts.<br /> <br /> But yes, as much as Garou love &quot;WOLF SMASH!&quot;, even they prefer to save the girl playing with the Talking Tina Doll or Chucky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T00:39:42-07:00","id":1464982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460695-the-apocalyptic-record-ks-has-begun?p=1464965#post1464965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything in the AR except Chapter 6 and the plot hooks sections are in character. Whatever the characters and storytellers in those section believe isn't objective truth and shouldn't be treated as such.<br /> <br /> I would draw your attention to the Philodox story hooks, which does say &quot;Even though no fallen Garou has ever redeemed doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s impossible. The time for such a miracle may be in the face of the coming Apocalypse.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit to add: I'm confused why you think W20 has an 'extremely hard no'. Not only do we have the words in the Philodox chapter as I've included above, W20 Umbra the Velvet Shadow included a BSD in Erebus working its way towards possible redemption. If anything, W20 has an extremely hard 'MAYBE' to it - ie, it's up to individual tables to decie if that's a story they want to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I thought the story hook sections were OOC. My mistake.<br /> <br /> Okay, the reason why I see it as a hard no is due to how W20 books handled the matter compared to Revised and 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> Previously, BSDs could be redeemed, there were even a rite and rules for it. This was a thing that was noted in multiple books. There was not one BSD working towards redemption, there were multiple ones that had passed Erebus to redemption.<br /> <br /> In W20, this was changed. In Book of the Wyrm, it was noted once you are a BSD, you are just beyond redemption. Then in the Umbra book, it is stated that a BSD is still being cooked in Erebus after many many decades. Then the philodox chapter with Wretch.<br /> <br /> Basically, compared to the previous canon, this all reads to me as a very hard no on redeeming BSDs. Looked within W20 context, it is a maybe. But from a wider context, it is a clear no or something EXTRA special.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T03:39:26-07:00","id":1464992,"title":"","content":"A handful that may have done it in the past by going through Erebus for unknown periods of time and torments, doesn't seem all that different from W20's take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T04:20:37-07:00","id":1464996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1460695-the-apocalyptic-record-ks-has-begun?p=1464992#post1464992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A handful that may have done it in the past by going through Erebus for unknown periods of time and torments, doesn't seem all that different from W20's take.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is different. Yes, a handful have come and faced torments for an unknown time in revised, but the W20 umbra book states that this -one- BSD has been in the river for -ages- and still isn't ready. Plus, in the BSD section of BoTW 20th edition, it is stated very clearly that the BSDs basically become Wyrmy puppets that cannot make choices against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Mind, this is not a BAD thing. It is just a change I do not agree with.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}